                <head>134. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On November 5, 1952, James S. Lay, Jr., Executive Secretary of the National
                    Security Council, transmitted a “Key Data Book” prepared by the NSC Reporting
                    Unit to President Truman. This briefing book contained sections on the national
                    psychological program and the foreign intelligence program. For text, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1952-54v02p1/pg_165"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1952–1954, volume II, Part 1, pages 165</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus:frus1952-54v02p1/pg_181">181</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
